@startuml 15-console-qml-handshake
!pragma layout smetana
' ConsoleBackend 与 QML 的 presentation/input 握手。
' 来源：GameView/console_backend.h/.cpp, qml/Console.qml, qml/ConsoleBlock.qml

title ConsoleBackend-QML：呈现确认与输入握手

participant "EraEngine / script" as E
participant "ConsoleBackend" as B
participant "SystemStateMachine" as S
participant "QML Console" as C
participant "Qt event loop" as Qt
participant "Stage/ListView" as V
participant "ConsoleBackend fallback" as F

E -> B : print / request input
B -> B : flush(), updateStageModels()
B -> B : generation++
B --> C : generationChanged()
B -> F : start 50ms presentationFallback
B --> C : presentationRequested()
C -> Qt : Qt.callLater(syncView, positionStage)
Qt -> C : deferred callback
C -> V : create delegates / sync model / position stage
V --> C : model/layout work handled
C -> B : notifyFramePresented()
B --> S : framePresented()
S -> S : onFramePresented()
B -> B : release presentation fallback

alt timed input
  B -> B : keep waitingInput=true; business timer not started before ack
  S -> E : start injected timer(timeout)
  E --> S : timeout callback
  S -> B : default input / resume
else ordinary input
  C -> B : submitInput(value/string/any-key/mouse)
  B -> B : validate kind + generation
  B --> E : inputSubmitted(value)
end

== generation and stale controls ==
E -> B : BREAKBUTTON / new generation
B -> B : generation++
B --> C : generationChanged()
C -> C : old button generation != backend.generation
C -> B : click(old button)
B --> C : ignore stale click

== destruction and fallback ==
C -> B : Component.onDestruction
B -> B : framePacingAttached=false
B -> F : arm presentationFallback
F --> B : timeout -> notifyFramePresented()
B --> S : framePresented()
S -> E : start injected timer(timeout)

note over B,C
  presentationRequested -> Qt.callLater -> model/stage handling ->
  notifyFramePresented is a layout/model acknowledgement. It does not prove
  a scene-graph swap or that pixels reached the display.
end note

note right of F
  This is ConsoleBackend::m_presentationFallback. It only releases the
  presentation acknowledgement path; the business timeout is the injected
  SystemStateMachine timer. A destroyed or unconnected QML view therefore
  cannot leave a timed wait armed forever.
end note

legend bottom
  generation is the backend's logical presentation version and button validity
  token. QML owns view composition and delegates; ConsoleBackend owns model,
  input state, and the handshake boundary.
endlegend
@enduml
